# Markdown preview laid out like GitHub: cmark-gfm HTML on a terminal cell grid, rendered off the main thread.
size 140x45
config
{"lsp": {"enabled": false}, "image_protocol": "none"}
end
copy README.md README.md
copy docs/screenshots/file-pane.png docs/screenshots/file-pane.png
copy docs/screenshots/welcome.png docs/screenshots/welcome.png
copy docs/screenshots/find-replace.png docs/screenshots/find-replace.png
copy docs/screenshots/lsp-errors.png docs/screenshots/lsp-errors.png
copy docs/screenshots/lsp-hover.png docs/screenshots/lsp-hover.png
copy docs/screenshots/diff.png docs/screenshots/diff.png
copy docs/screenshots/terminal.png docs/screenshots/terminal.png
copy docs/DESIGN.md DESIGN.md
file tour.md
# Tour

Jump to [the alert](#an-alert), or open the [README](README.md).

## Details

<details>
<summary>Click to expand</summary>

Hidden until the summary is clicked.

</details>

## A table

| Key | Action | Notes |
|:-------|:-------:|-------:|
| Alt+p | preview | the full overlay |
| Ctrl+s | save | atomic, mode kept |

## Nested

1. First item
   - a bullet
     - a deeper bullet
2. Second item
   > a quote inside the list
   > > and a quote inside that

## An alert

> [!TIP]
> Alerts render like GitHub: a colored title and bar.

## Filler

Paragraph one keeps the page long enough to scroll.

Paragraph two keeps the page long enough to scroll.

Paragraph three keeps the page long enough to scroll.

Paragraph four keeps the page long enough to scroll.

Paragraph five keeps the page long enough to scroll.

Paragraph six keeps the page long enough to scroll.

Paragraph seven keeps the page long enough to scroll.

Paragraph eight keeps the page long enough to scroll.

Paragraph nine keeps the page long enough to scroll.

Paragraph ten keeps the page long enough to scroll.
end
run tour.md
wait # Tour
key alt+p
wait A table
snap table A pipe table: GitHub-style borders with a rule between rows, bold header, columns aligned left, center and right.
snap nested Nested lists and quotes: bullets change with depth, a quote inside a list item keeps its indent, a nested quote gets a second bar.
snap details-closed A closed details block shows only its summary.
click 16 14
wait Hidden until the summary
snap details-open Clicking the summary opens it in place; the scroll position stays.
click 20 9
wait Alerts render like
snap anchor Clicking an anchor link scrolls the heading it names to the top: the alert, with its colored title and bar.
key alt+,
wait Jump to the alert, or
snap back Alt+, goes back to where the link was clicked.
click 45 9
wait written in Odin, inspired by micro
snap readme A link to another markdown file opens it in the preview.
key pgdn down*10
wait Welcome screen: working root
snap readme-grid The README screenshot table keeps its two columns, each cell an image (its alt text here, without kitty graphics) with the caption under it.
key esc
wait-gone click a link to open it
key ctrl+p
type toggle split
wait Markdown: Toggle Split
key enter
wait-gone Toggle
wheel 20 20 up 30
wait written in Odin, inspired by micro
wheel 20 20 down 8
wait-gone written in Odin, inspired by micro
snap scroll-sync In the split, wheeling the editor scrolls the preview to the same source line.
key alt+f
type DESIGN.md
wait DESIGN.md  
key enter
wait Data model
type Typing
wait Typing# qed
snap typing Typing into the 1000-line DESIGN.md: the text lands at once and the preview catches up a moment later, rendered on its own thread.
